# Scientific Integrity — Pre-Registration and Honest Claims

## Pre-register before results exist
Any confirmatory comparison gets its numeric acceptance threshold **committed to the repo as a spec file BEFORE the results are generated** (pattern: `GATE_SPEC.md`, committed before the 90 gate cells landed).

The **M3.5 dissolving arm** is the next live case: the acceptance criterion is pre-registered in `GATE_SPEC.md §DA1` (committed 2026-07-05, before any M3.5 cells exist). Threshold: |mean ΔAUROC| < 0.02 (matches C1 gate tolerance). The rule is the discipline; `GATE_SPEC.md` is the falsifiable artifact.

**Never expand-and-re-judge to force a pass.** A failed pre-registered criterion is a finding, not a bug to iterate away. (Pattern: C3 shortfall was root-caused and reported as a credible partial reproduction — not re-gated until green.)

**C1+C2 vs C3 scope:** only C1 (mean AUROC) and C2 (Spearman rank) are hard stops that block the pipeline. C3 (per-dataset band) failure alone does not block — it is reported as a finding. Do not treat C3 failure as a reason to stop or re-run.

## Claims must track recorded metadata
The A/B is **same-family, same-size** — mode A = base+LoRA, mode B = frozen instruct — `checkpoint_kind` recorded in every cell's metadata. **Never let paper or plan prose regress to "same-model" or "same weights"** — a reviewer can falsify that from our own JSONs.

Security results rest on 2 datasets. Always phrase as suggestive per-dataset evidence, never as a Friedman-backed generalization (no statistical power at n=2–3). Correct framing example:

> "On credit-card fraud and UNSW-NB15, we observe..." ✓  
> "LLMs generalize to security data" ✗  
> "Across security domains, LLMs show..." ✗

## Before submission
Every specific claim about what a cited paper did must be verified against the **primary PDF**, not a secondhand summary. Facts already verified live in `docs/claude/memory/anollm-verified-facts.md` and `related-work-verified.md` — cite from there, and flag anything not yet independently verified with a `TODO: verify-vs-PDF` comment in the draft.
